# civil-holidays-well-known v1
# source: spoken-aliases
# retrieved: 2026-07-22
# note:
#   CURATED SPOKEN ALIASES for the globally well-known holiday set (see
#   chronologia.civil_holidays.WELL_KNOWN). Each row lists the colloquial names
#   a person actually SAYS for a holiday in one language - the surfaces the
#   `holiday_ref` extraction construction binds ("christmas", "when is easter",
#   "next christmas"). These are spoken forms kept as data, deliberately
#   distinct from the official native names (in the per-jurisdiction .tab files)
#   and the display translations (translations.tab). The engine harvests these
#   at LangSpec-load time, unioned with the anchor holiday's translation and its
#   own official native name, and folds them through the same normaliser the
#   matcher uses. Surfaces carry their real orthography (accents included), and
#   colloquial/short forms (xmas, Weihnachten) live here.
# columns: key | lang | surface ;; surface ;; ...
#
# ===== English =====
new_year        | en | new year's day ;; new years day
new_year_eve    | en | new year's eve ;; new years eve
epiphany        | en | epiphany ;; three kings day
carnival        | en | carnival ;; mardi gras
good_friday     | en | good friday
easter          | en | easter ;; easter sunday
easter_monday   | en | easter monday
ascension       | en | ascension ;; ascension day
pentecost       | en | pentecost ;; whitsun ;; whit sunday
whit_monday     | en | whit monday ;; pentecost monday
corpus_christi  | en | corpus christi
assumption      | en | assumption ;; assumption day
all_saints      | en | all saints day ;; all saints' day
christmas_eve   | en | christmas eve
christmas       | en | christmas ;; christmas day ;; xmas
boxing_day      | en | boxing day
